WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.571
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:09.199
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.499 --> 00:00:16.679
Unit nineteen: Speaking Test: Interview and Discussion. Today you will answer questions clearly and give reasons.

4
00:00:16.979 --> 00:00:19.562
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.209
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:25.958
Interview.

7
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:30.157
Interview means a formal conversation with questions.

8
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.274
The interview begins.

9
00:00:32.883 --> 00:00:35.280
Your turn. Say: Interview.

10
00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:38.983
Interview.

11
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.530
Fluent.

12
00:00:41.517 --> 00:00:43.493
Fluent means speaking smoothly.

13
00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:45.212
She is fluent.

14
00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:48.167
Your turn. Say: Fluent.

15
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:51.814
Fluent.

16
00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.354
Pause.

17
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:55.990
Pause means a short stop.

18
00:00:56.583 --> 00:00:58.095
Use a short pause.

19
00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:01.196
Your turn. Say: Pause.

20
00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:05.116
Pause.

21
00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:06.747
Opinion.

22
00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.575
Opinion means a personal view.

23
00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:11.324
Give your opinion.

24
00:01:11.917 --> 00:01:14.348
Your turn. Say: Opinion.

25
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.131
Opinion.

26
00:01:18.883 --> 00:01:19.733
Reason.

27
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.645
Reason means why you think this.

28
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.356
Give a reason.

29
00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.022
Your turn. Say: Reason.

30
00:01:29.867 --> 00:01:30.728
Reason.

31
00:01:31.483 --> 00:01:32.333
Agree.

32
00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.350
Agree means to have the same view.

33
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.056
I agree with you.

34
00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.558
Your turn. Say: Agree.

35
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.355
Agree.

36
00:01:45.117 --> 00:01:46.164
Disagree.

37
00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:49.242
Disagree means to have a different view.

38
00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.478
I disagree politely.

39
00:01:52.083 --> 00:01:55.281
Your turn. Say: Disagree.

40
00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.065
Disagree.

41
00:01:59.817 --> 00:02:00.945
Elaborate.

42
00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.112
Elaborate means to give more detail.

43
00:02:04.717 --> 00:02:05.996
Please elaborate.

44
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:09.131
Your turn. Say: Elaborate.

45
00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:12.991
Elaborate.

46
00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.288
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:21.125
Visal, how do I answer a speaking question?

48
00:02:22.217 --> 00:02:33.533
Answer directly, then give a reason and an example. For instance, I like reading because it helps me learn. Last week I read an interesting story about space.

49
00:02:34.617 --> 00:02:36.349
What if I do not know a word?

50
00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:48.487
Do not stop. Use other words to explain it: It is a thing that you use to cut paper. Short natural pauses are fine, and so are phrases like Let me think.

51
00:02:49.583 --> 00:02:51.455
How do I disagree politely?

52
00:02:52.550 --> 00:03:03.413
Use phrases such as I see your point, but I think and I am afraid I disagree. Always give a reason. Listen to the other person and respond to what they say.

53
00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:06.067
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:06.917 --> 00:03:09.857
Grammar focus: answer, reason, example.

55
00:03:10.157 --> 00:03:11.402
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:12.117 --> 00:03:14.662
I like reading because it helps me learn.

57
00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:18.374
I see your point, but I think it is too expensive.

58
00:03:19.333 --> 00:03:26.328
Answer directly, give a reason and an example, and keep speaking if you forget a word. Disagree politely with a reason.

59
00:03:27.083 --> 00:03:31.468
Be careful! Don't say: I do not know. (silence)

60
00:03:33.433 --> 00:03:36.025
Say: I describe the word I forgot.

61
00:03:36.325 --> 00:03:37.523
Keep speaking.

62
00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:41.044
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:41.833 --> 00:03:42.834
The Interview.

64
00:03:43.134 --> 00:03:45.111
Piseth is in a speaking interview.

65
00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.471
The examiner asks about his hobbies.

66
00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.745
He answers directly and gives a reason.

67
00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:55.511
He forgets a word, so he describes it.

68
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.941
He thanks the examiner politely at the end.

69
00:04:00.033 --> 00:04:03.942
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:04.783 --> 00:04:06.098
First you should blank.

71
00:04:06.398 --> 00:04:10.794
A, leave. B, answer directly. C, stay silent.

72
00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:16.577
The answer is B: answer directly.

73
00:04:17.717 --> 00:04:19.496
A reason begins with blank.

74
00:04:19.796 --> 00:04:22.973
A, but. B, never. C, because.

75
00:04:26.533 --> 00:04:28.591
The answer is C: because.

76
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.715
If you forget a word, you can blank.

77
00:04:32.015 --> 00:04:35.993
A, describe it. B, stop. C, cry.

78
00:04:39.533 --> 00:04:41.672
The answer is A: describe it.

79
00:04:42.817 --> 00:04:44.805
To disagree politely use blank.

80
00:04:45.105 --> 00:04:49.582
A, No way. B, I see your point, but. C, You are wrong.

81
00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:55.330
The answer is B: I see your point, but.

82
00:04:56.483 --> 00:04:58.599
Who asks Piseth questions?

83
00:04:58.899 --> 00:05:02.738
A, his friend. B, his mother. C, the examiner.

84
00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.601
The answer is C: the examiner.

85
00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:12.963
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:13.817 --> 00:05:15.900
What is your hobby? Why?

87
00:05:24.717 --> 00:05:26.194
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:26.494 --> 00:05:36.289
My hobby is reading because it helps me learn new words. Last week I read a story about a brave girl. I enjoy it because it makes me think.

89
00:05:36.589 --> 00:05:38.229
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:39.117 --> 00:05:43.534
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and answer, reason, example.

91
00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:47.659
Today's value is confidence. Speak up and be proud of who you are.

92
00:05:47.959 --> 00:05:50.518
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

93
00:05:50.818 --> 00:05:53.505
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

